   "note_tweet": {
    "text": "i have been searching for quite some time, but i haven‘t found a single web3 company worth looking into, and the zk space is not advanced enough yet. all other web3 stuff is effectively just people investing into imaginary units of value, i.e. actually bringing people much further away from „money that works“. After all, there‘s still no core banking platform which is truly rooted in zk-enabled web3. And as long as no real licensed bank is based on such a system, money also won‘t become easier. People always think that making money easier needs innovations, but that‘s not true! It rather needs careful excavation of the structures which form *today‘s* money, and then the engagement and money of many people to create the interface between yesterday‘s money and tomorrow‘s money. No one else will do it for us"
